<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Grey League</h1><p class="st-meta">1395 CE – 1799 CE · capital Ilanz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The largest of the Three Leagues of the Grisons, a federation of upper Rhine valley communes sworn under a maple tree at Truns in 1424.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1395 the abbot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/disentis-abbey">Disentis</a> and local lords of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> valley made an alliance for peace and mutual protection, and in 1424 it was renewed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trun">Truns</a>, under a maple tree, as a league that included the communes themselves. The name Grey League is traditionally explained by the grey homespun cloth worn by its people.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The league joined communes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surselva">Surselva</a>, Hinterrhein and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesolcina">Mesolcina</a> valleys, each with its own courts and assembly, meeting at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilanz">Ilanz</a>. It allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-gods-house">League of God's House</a> in 1406 and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-the-ten-jurisdictions">League of the Ten Jurisdictions</a> in 1471, forming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/three-leagues">Three Leagues</a>, and in 1497 became an associate of the Swiss. Its communes divided between Catholic and Reformed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/three-leagues">Grisons</a> became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a> in 1799 and a Swiss canton in 1803. The league's name survives in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graubunden">Graubünden</a>, the canton's German name.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/grey-league.jpg" alt="Grey League" width="320" height="299"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (sidonius 15:49, 30 June 2006 (UTC)) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trois_ligues.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1395 CE – 1799 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ilanz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Reformed Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Romansh, German, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Switzerland</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Grauer Bund, Upper League, Ligia Grischa</dd></dl></aside></div>

